From: LuneOS port <webos-ports@webos-ports.org>
Subject: [PATCH] gslX680: build the Silead point-id algorithm object again

mtk_gslX680.c references gsl_alg_id_main/gsl_mask_tiaoping/
gsl_obtain_gesture, which live in the (GPL-licensed C) point-id file
whose obj-y line was commented out — vmlinux fails to link with
CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_MTK_GSLX680=y, and stock enables it.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor driver, no upstream]
---
diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/mediatek/gslX680/mt6739/Makefile b/drivers/input/touchscreen/mediatek/gslX680/mt6739/Makefile
index 25df9ba8b157..10134b078518 100755
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/mediatek/gslX680/mt6739/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/mediatek/gslX680/mt6739/Makefile
@@ -3,5 +3,5 @@
 ccflags-y += -I$(srctree)/drivers/input/touchscreen/mediatek/
 ccflags-y += -I$(srctree)/drivers/misc/mediatek/include/mt-plat/
 
-# obj-y   +=  gsl_point_id_point_active_pen_no_gesture.o
+obj-y   +=  gsl_point_id_point_active_pen_no_gesture.o
 obj-y	+=  mtk_gslX680.o
